its straight quotation marks into curly ones, and the field had no way to say
no. The field takes HTML's `autocorrect`, and off turns off every rewrite the
platform makes as somebody types: autocorrect, spell checking, predictions, and
iOS's smart quotes, dashes and spacing. Unset, each platform derives it from
the keyboard type as it did.

